  "limitations": [
    "One active request per profile; the lane ships --max-concurrency 1 and no concurrency claim is made.",
    "Automatic checkpoints remain best effort under live traffic. Transient refusals retry up to six times per completed turn, and admission saves a session's newest turn before evicting it, but a crash or an expired graceful wait can still leave unpublished work unsaved. The measured restart gate proves the two short target sessions survived, not globally loss-free shutdown.",
    "Save-before-evict with ceiling-class sessions was exercised on the RTX 5090 only (releases/v0.8.0/qualification/rtx5090.json, docs/measurements/2026-09-24-durable-session-eviction.json, docs/measurements/2026-09-24-publication-barrier.json). This lane's source b0e8c2fa differs from the RTX 5090's 86733c0e only by the Windows-only commit precharge margin before pinned host allocations; its window runs its own phases and did not construct a ceiling-class eviction.",
    "Restore may reclaim a resident session only when its latest checkpoint is reproducible. Restore and response-store capacity refusal remain possible. The qualified 11264 MiB host-KV pool and 32768 MiB declared host-memory floor are unchanged; no smaller-host profile is qualified.",
    "A managed start could fail when the driver refused to pin the 11264 MiB host-KV pool (alphastorm/omp-ninfer#48): the pin charges its size and then a page-lock remainder, and a start whose free commit covered only the size raced the system-managed pagefile extension. The v0.6.7-beta.2 candidate 86733c0e was refused this way on its first managed start after a fresh install. b0e8c2fa commits and releases each pinned allocation's size plus 1/64 first, and this lane's canonical qualification passed that first start. The refusal was never reproduced on demand, so the issue stays open until field confirmation; a recurrence reports the commit limit, available commit and available memory.",
    "The C1 benchmark fixture (28,000 characters of one repeated sentence) is trajectory-sensitive: its acceptance and decode rate move with changes in prefill summation order or fixture length (docs/measurements/2026-09-13-rtx4090-c1-fixture-sensitivity.json).",
    "Measured numbers apply only to this package, this machine, and this profile."
  ],
